cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this app, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references.
type: software
title: iEEG Spectral & Connectivity Features
abstract: Per-channel spectral and connectivity features of intracranial EEG recordings, following Bernabei et al.
  2022 (band-pass 0.5-80 Hz, resampling to 200 Hz, Welch PSD with 2 s Hamming windows and 50% overlap; band power
  as absolute power, relative power and the median of the sum-normalised spectrum; magnitude-squared coherence
  between channel pairs from 1 s windows, averaged over each band, and each channel's mean coherence), written in a
  shared long feature table; one step of the Interictal Biomarker Mapping workflow.
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
repository-code: https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/processor-ieeg-bandpower
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
- ieeg
- seeg
- electrophysiology
- epilepsy
- spectral-analysis
- band-power
- coherence
